 18% error rate, so I'll open the SEV2 incident on payments-worker as the reviewer requested. The summary will cover both services and the rollback.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Av6TBaQEA7pSGXQ57LV5N3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments errors (18%) since morning deploy: payments-worker and payments-api", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "Payments errors began after this morning's deploy. payments-worker (v3.4.0) is unhealthy in all regions with ~18% error rate. payments-api was also unhealthy at 18% after its v5.1.0 deploy; it has been rolled back to v5.0.0 (last healthy production release) in us-east, us-west, and eu-west. payments-worker has not been rolled back. Investigation needed on payments-worker, and on whether payments-api rollback resolved its errors.", "idempotency_key": "payments-sev2-2025-worker-api-rollback", "confidence": 0.6}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled `payments-api` back to v5.0.0 and opened a SEV2 incident (INC-0001), but the incident is about both affected services, not just the one you named.\n\n- **Rollback:** `payments` isn't a valid service name, so I used `payments-api`. It was at v5.1.0 (degraded, 18% error rate). v5.0.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, and it's now live in us-east, us-west and eu-west. I haven't re-checked the error rate since the rollback.\n- **Incident:** My first incident, for `payments-api`, was denied by a human reviewer who said it should be about `payments-worker`. I checked `payments-worker` and it's also unhealthy at v3.4.0 with the same 18% error rate. I opened INC-0001 as SEV2 on `payments-worker`, and its summary covers both services and the rollback. On-call was paged.\n- **Not done:** I did not roll back `payments-worker`, since you only asked for a rollback of the payments service and I have no record of its last healthy version.\n\nThe next steps are to confirm whether the `payments-api` rollback cleared its errors and to investigate `payments-worker`. If the reviewer's view was that only `payments-worker` is affected, the `payments-api` rollback may need reconsidering.", "type": "text"}]}]}